Notes:
  - 'effective TFLOPS' is approximate (counts only the dominant fp
    ops in the inner loop). Useful for relative comparison across
    stacks at matched config; not a substitute for jax.profiler.trace.
  - 'util %' compares to RTX 5090's 104.8 TFLOPS fp32 peak.
    Saturating to >50%% requires:
      • enough threads in flight (>= ~1M for 5090's 21504 cores)
      • compute-bound (not memory-bound) inner loop
      • no host syncs blocking the stream
  - JAX `block_until_ready` is the analogue of CUDA's synchronize().
